// Logline: 11 sibling role audit files do not yet exist on disk; the 2026-08-19 wave is producing them in parallel. This file records the disjoint-write contract from x86_phalanx.oot §4, the Wave 1 -> 2 -> 3 run order from §5, and the empty results table that fills in after Wave 1 lands.
//
// Setup: Read-only review of openOODA/audit/x86_phalanx.oot (master 12-role plan, §4 and §5). C emit + gcc is the everyday path. x86 is the side emit, not a complete backend. Side binary at oodac/oodac.x86; do not write oodac/oodac. Other agents are reading x86_phalanx.oot and writing their own audit paths in parallel.
//
// Beats:
//   1. Restate the 12 roles and disjoint writes from x86_phalanx.oot §4.
//   2. State the Wave 1 -> 2 -> 3 run order from x86_phalanx.oot §5.
//   3. List sibling audit files on disk NOW.
//   4. Check disjoint writes: no role owns two audit paths.
//   5. List the empty results table; it fills in after Wave 1.
//   6. State what COORD does not touch and the rebuild rules.

