Per-role audit files (per the 2026-08-19 task sheet; the
phalanx §4 names only the 8 audit files PV1..HYG and DOCS
and COORD, so the per-role mapping below is from the task
sheet, not the phalanx §4):

  DE1   -> openOODA/audit/x86_de1.oot
  DE2   -> openOODA/audit/x86_de2.oot
  RT    -> openOODA/audit/x86_rt.oot
  PV1   -> openOODA/audit/x86_pv1.oot
  PV2   -> openOODA/audit/x86_pv2.oot
  SEC   -> openOODA/audit/x86_sec.oot
  MEM   -> openOODA/audit/x86_mem.oot
  INT   -> openOODA/audit/x86_int.oot
  HARN  -> openOODA/audit/x86_harn.oot
  HYG   -> openOODA/audit/x86_hyg.oot
  DOCS  -> openOODA/audit/x86_docs.oot
  COORD -> openOODA/audit/x86_coord.oot

Disjoint writes: each role owns one write path (product
code OR audit OR fixture/smoke OR board). The two
DOCS-owned boards (SHIPPED.oot, ROADMAP.oot) are exclusive
to DOCS; no other role touches them. No two audit roles
share an audit file. Review roles (PV1, PV2, SEC, MEM,
HARN, INT, HYG) write only their audit file.


COORD writes only openOODA/audit/x86_coord.oot (this file).
COORD does not edit SHIPPED.oot or ROADMAP.oot. COORD does
not rebuild. COORD does not touch product emit, fixtures,
or smokes.

// ============================================================
// 2. Run order (per x86_phalanx.oot §5)
// ============================================================

Per x86_phalanx.oot:117-127 (Subagent waves):

  Wave 1 (builders + harness fixtures) — parallel
    DE1, DE2, RT, HARN
    HARN writes x86_hello_smoke; do not flip open69 yet.

  Wave 2 (adversarial) — after Wave 1 files exist
    PV1, PV2, SEC, MEM

  Wave 3 (prove + boards) — after one side rebuild
    INT, HYG, DOCS, COORD rollup

Isolation: none (no worktree). Disjoint files. No race
rebuilds. Rebuild: side binary only, oodac/oodac.x86.
PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1 only if the host cannot check new helpers.
Do not write oodac/oodac (x86_phalanx.oot:127-129).
Smokes that must run emit-x86 prefer ./oodac/oodac.x86 if
executable, else ./oodac/oodac (x86_phalanx.oot:130-131).

Anti-pattern: two agents on the same stuck as/ld failure
(x86_phalanx.oot:133).

