// ============================================================
// 6. COORD does not touch
// ============================================================

Per x86_phalanx.oot:6-7, 115, 126-132, 138-145:

  No .py .sh .md .js.
  No c_emit*.oo (including c_emit_secret_check.oo).
  No llvm_emit*.oo. No wasm_emit*.oo.
  No lex/parse/check/tc. No main.oo. No cli_emit.oo.
  No cli_build.oo. No runtime/chs_rt*.c.
  No guide/ or registry HTML.
  Do not copy bin/ooda onto oodac/oodac.
  Do not claim AArch64. Do not retire C emit + gcc.
  Do not edit SHIPPED.oot or ROADMAP.oot.
  Do not write oodac/oodac. Do not race a second rebuild.
  Do not git commit unless asked.
  COORD does not run emit. COORD does not run smokes.

// ============================================================
// 7. Wave 1 deps and handoff
// ============================================================

Wave 1 must produce, on disk:
  ooda/oodac/x86_emit.oo                  (exists, 61 lines)
  ooda/oodac/x86_emit_fold.oo             (exists, 192 lines)
  ooda/oodac/x86_emit_sys.oo              (exists, 68 lines)
  ooda/scripts/x86_hello_smoke.oo         (exists, 56 lines)
  Audit files for DE1, DE2, RT, HARN       (this turn or later)

When those four audit files land, Wave 2 (PV1, PV2, SEC,
MEM) starts. Each Wave 2 role reads only the Wave 1 product
code; none of them edit it. The PV1 fixtures (x86_empty.oo,
x86_nomain.oo) are part of Wave 1 deliverables; absent now
means Wave 1 has not yet landed.

After Wave 2, the parent rebuilds oodac/oodac.x86 with
PURE_SKIP_CHECK=1 only if the host cannot check new helpers
(x86_phalanx.oot:128). Then Wave 3 runs INT and HYG; INT
re-runs existing locks (SHIPPED.oot:34 names them), HYG
counts lines. DOCS and COORD finalize. INT confirms the
locks named on SHIPPED.oot:34 and ROADMAP.oot:43 still
pass; HYG reports any file over 256 lines; DOCS audits the
boards; COORD reports the disjoint-write status here.

